{
  "id": "noodle-stall",
  "name": "Noodle Stall",
  "description": "Hae's Noodles, a street stall built into the ground floor of an old building on Level 4 of the Ribbon, right under Lowlight Intake. A deep worn wooden counter with five stools, a striped dark-red awning with red paper lanterns, and behind it the cramped kitchen: the stockpot that's never off, ladles and strainers on hooks, stacked bowls, jars of chilli and pickles. A red neon bowl-and-chopsticks sign with no words, because everyone on the level knows what it is. Above the awning, the Intake's big window glows late behind half-drawn blinds, a desk lamp and a shelf of binders, and a narrow stair climbs the side of the building to its door. An old vending machine hums at the foot of the stairs; beside the stall, an alley runs round the back past Hae's kitchen door. Overhead, the walkway of the level above, and far up through the gap, a cyan planet sign on a tower.",
